# SDD §14 — Firefox is the company default browser.
#
# /etc/xdg is the sysadmin tier of the XDG association spec: it outranks the
# vendor defaults in /usr/share/applications/mimeapps.list, and a user's own
# ~/.config/mimeapps.list still outranks this — so GNOME Settings > Default
# Applications keeps working. That is the intended three-tier split (SDD §14):
# a company default, not a lock.
#
# Firefox rather than Chrome: Mozilla publishes and Flathub verifies the Firefox
# build, while com.google.Chrome is community packaging around Google's binary.
# Both are installed; only the default differs.
#
# The .desktop id is the Flatpak app id, which does not exist in the image —
# first boot installs it. An association naming a missing .desktop is inert, so
# this is safe to ship ahead of the app. 50-desktop.sh validates the id against
# config/desktop/system-flatpaks.list.
[Default Applications]
x-scheme-handler/http=org.mozilla.firefox.desktop
x-scheme-handler/https=org.mozilla.firefox.desktop
x-scheme-handler/about=org.mozilla.firefox.desktop
x-scheme-handler/unknown=org.mozilla.firefox.desktop
text/html=org.mozilla.firefox.desktop
application/xhtml+xml=org.mozilla.firefox.desktop
